---
// The landing page: the pitch and install, how a review works, the deck, install for each harness,
// and the status.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Deck from '../components/Deck.astro'

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<Base
  title="parley"
  description="parley shows an agent's plan as a page. You answer its questions there, and it reads your answers from a file."
>
  <main class="page">
    <section>
      <h1>parley</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        parley shows an agent's plan as a page. You answer its questions there, and it reads your
        answers from a file.
      </p>
      <pre><code>claude plugin marketplace add osdlc/parley
claude plugin install parley@parley</code></pre>
      <p class="aside">
        That is Claude Code. <a href="#harnesses">Codex, Cursor and Pi</a> are below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Write.</strong> The agent writes a document as JSON.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Check.</strong>
          <code>parley check</code> rejects a broken document.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review.</strong> You comment and answer its questions on one page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Read back.</strong> The agent reads your answers from a JSON file and revises.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The deck</h2>
      <div class="deck-frame">
        <Deck deck="launch" embedded />
      </div>
      <p class="deck-links">
        Click the deck, then use the arrow keys. <a href={`${base}slides/launch/`}>Full screen</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="harnesses">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>
        One marketplace, osdlc/parley, serves all four harnesses. The plugin id is
        <code>parley@parley</code>. Node 22 or later, Bun or Deno; nothing else to install.
      </p>

      <h3>Claude Code</h3>
      <pre><code>claude plugin marketplace add osdlc/parley
claude plugin install parley@parley</code></pre>
      <p>
        In a session, the same is <code>/plugin marketplace add osdlc/parley</code>, then
        <code>/plugin install parley@parley</code>. A skill runs as
        <code>/parley:&lt;skill&gt;</code> in Claude Code.
      </p>

      <h3>Codex</h3>
      <pre><code>codex plugin marketplace add osdlc/parley
codex plugin add parley@parley</code></pre>

      <h3>Cursor</h3>
      <pre><code>cursor-agent plugin marketplace add https://github.com/osdlc/parley</code></pre>
      <p>
        This adds the marketplace to your Cursor account. <code>cursor-agent</code> has no install
        command: install <code>parley</code> in the Cursor app, which lists the plugins of your
        marketplaces.
      </p>

      <h3>Pi</h3>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/osdlc/parley
pi install ./parley/.pi/packs/parley</code></pre>
      <p>
        Pi installs from a folder and records its path, so keep the clone where it is. Skills run as
        <code>/skill:parley-&lt;skill&gt;</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Status</h2>
      <p>
        Alpha. The file format may change. One reviewer at a time. It runs on your machine, and by
        default nothing leaves it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer>parley</footer>
  </main>
</Base>
